@startuml sequence_diagram_direct_url_access
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - WEB03 Direct URL Access to a Protected Section (e.g. /manage/stock typed in the address bar)

actor User as "Client / User"
participant Router as "AppRoutes\n(router, WEB01)"
participant Guard as "ProtectedRoute\n(AA03, extended)"
participant Access as "accessPolicy"
participant Auth as "AuthProvider"
participant Page as "StockPage\n(WEB05)"
participant API as "apiClient"
participant BE as "Back-End API\nAuthMiddleware + RoleMiddleware"

note over User, BE
    The menu (SD 1) only HIDES options. This diagram shows the check that runs whenever a section
    is requested by URL, bookmark, browser history or an in-app link (AC 2, AC 3, AC 7).
    Section "stock": access = "protected", roles = [MANAGER] (navigationPolicy, Table 1).
    The page component is mounted ONLY on ALLOW: on every other decision no protected request is made.
end note

User -> Router : types /manage/stock and presses Enter
activate Router
Router -> Router : findSectionByPath("/manage/stock")

alt A) Path does not match any section
    Router --> User : NotFoundPage (WEB02)
    note right of Router : interaction ends

else B) Section "stock" found
    Router -> Guard : render(section = stock)
    activate Guard
    Guard -> Access : evaluateAccess(stock, auth)
    activate Access
    Access -> Auth : status, hasAnyRole("MANAGER")
    Auth --> Access : state
    Access --> Guard : decision
    deactivate Access

    alt B1) PENDING (status = "loading": /auth/me still running)
        Guard --> User : loading indicator (WEB04)\nno page, no business request
        note right of Guard : re-evaluated when AuthProvider\nfinishes loading

    else B2) LOGIN_REQUIRED (status = "guest")
        Guard -> Router : navigate("/login?returnTo=/manage/stock", { replace: true })
        Router --> User : LoginPage (AA01 / AA02)
        note right of Router
            returnTo carries ONLY the path (no token, no data, AA04 AC 6).
            After login, LoginPage navigates to returnTo only if
            navigationPolicy.isSafeReturnPath(returnTo) (internal path of a
            known section); otherwise to "/". The guard runs again there.
        end note

    else B3) ACCOUNT_DENIED (status = "denied": inactive account / no role, AA03)
        Guard --> User : AccessDeniedPage(auth.deniedMessage)

    else B4) Authenticated: roles must be confirmed before the page is mounted
        Guard -> Auth : refresh()
        activate Auth
        Auth -> API : GET /api/v1/auth/me\n(skipAuthFailureHandler = true: answer mapped\nby AuthProvider, never by the global handler)
        activate API
        API -> BE : GET /api/v1/auth/me (Bearer)
        activate BE
        BE --> API : 200 { roles, active } / 401 / 403 / 5xx
        deactivate BE
        API --> Auth : result
        deactivate API
        Auth -> Auth : update currentUser / status (as in SD 1)
        Auth --> Guard : state changed
        deactivate Auth
        Guard -> Access : evaluateAccess(stock, auth)
        activate Access
        Access --> Guard : decision
        deactivate Access

        alt B4a) FORBIDDEN (e.g. roles = [CUSTOMER] or [EMPLOYEE] or [ADMINISTRATOR])
            Guard --> User : AccessDeniedPage("You do not have permission\nto access this page.")
            note right of Guard
                StockPage is NOT mounted: no stock data is requested
                or rendered. The message does not reveal the section's
                content, the required roles or the user's roles (AC 3).
                Link "Back to start" (WEB02).
            end note

        else B4b) LOGIN_REQUIRED / ACCOUNT_DENIED (refresh answered 401 / 403 / 5xx)
            Guard --> User : LoginPage / AccessDeniedPage (same as B2 / B3)

        else B4c) ALLOW (roles contain MANAGER, e.g. [MANAGER] or [CUSTOMER, MANAGER])
            Guard -> Page : mount
            activate Page
            Page -> API : GET /api/v1/stock
            activate API
            API -> BE : GET /api/v1/stock (Bearer)
            activate BE
            BE -> BE : verifyToken -> resolveActor (roles from DB)\n-> requireRole("MANAGER")
            note right of BE
                Back-end check on the SAME request (AC 7, AA05):
                if the role was removed meanwhile -> 403,
                handled as in SD 3.
            end note
            BE --> API : 200 OK { stock page }
            deactivate BE
            API --> Page : data
            deactivate API
            Page --> User : stock section (current section highlighted, WEB02)
            deactivate Page
        end
    end
    deactivate Guard
end

deactivate Router

@enduml